Root cause found by probing a running 0.4.15 instance: GET /api/settings/connect returned the settings JSON while /api/settings/connect/ returned index.html with 200. axum 0.8 nest("/connect") + route("/") matches only the slash-less path; the outer .fallback(serve_frontend) caught the slash form and served the SPA. The PR's Playwright test mocked **/api/** so it never touched the real router, and the server test only exercised a path rejected by auth middleware before routing. /api/settings/instance/ had the same latent bug since instance auth landed. Chose to fix the client paths and make serve_frontend return a JSON 404 for api/* rather than add NormalizePath: a router-level .layer runs after routing so it would not help, and wrapping the whole service changes every route. The JSON 404 makes any future wrong API path fail visibly instead of as a JSON parse error. Verified the new router test fails without the fallback change.
